# ALS Audit Station configuration — TEMPLATE.
# Copy to the USB root as audit.conf and fill in. The real audit.conf is
# gitignored because it holds credentials; keep this file secret-free.

# ALS Inventory — Hardware Audit tool config.
# Read by hardware-audit.sh so runs need no login or network typed each time.
# Keep this file next to hardware-audit.sh on the USB.

AUDIT_URL="https://als-inventory-software-production.up.railway.app"

# --- account ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Use a DEDICATED STATION ACCOUNT, never a person's login and never an admin.
# This password sits in plaintext on a USB stick in a warehouse: if the stick
# walks, an admin credential walks with it. A station account limits the blast
# radius to exactly what the station does.
#
# Create it once in ALS Inventory (Users -> New User):
#   Role:        technician
#   Permissions: UNTICK everything, then tick exactly these three -
#                  * Goods In
#                  * Perform Amazon Audit
#                  * Perform Goods In Audit
# That covers every call the station makes (lot picker, prior-audit lookup,
# sub-lot picker, and filing audits in both workflows) and NOTHING else - no
# reports, no selling, no deleting, no user management. Granting only ONE of
# the two audit permissions makes a single-workflow station: the chooser
# disappears and every audit files to that workflow.
AUDIT_EMAIL="station@your-domain"
AUDIT_PASSWORD=""

# --- operator (who did the wipe) -----------------------------------------------
# The operator types their name on the kiosk screen. Wipes are filed with the
# station account above, and the certificate prints that name as
# "Operator (self-declared)" next to the filing account.
#
# Planned, NOT YET IMPLEMENTED: operators signing in on the kiosk with their
# own ALS Inventory login (owner decision D27, to be switched by an
# AUDIT_OPERATOR_SIGNIN setting). No kiosk reads that setting yet - adding it
# to audit.conf has NO effect: wipes do not wait for a sign-in and are still
# filed under the station account. It will be documented here when it ships.

# --- admin PIN ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Guards the kiosk's Settings screen. WITHOUT one, the server address, image
# server and wipe method cannot be changed from the screen at all (Wi-Fi still
# can). Pick one, and keep it off the stick's label.
AUDIT_ADMIN_PIN=""

# Wi-Fi to connect to automatically at the start of each run.
# Leave WIFI_SSID blank if you use a wired/Ethernet connection.
WIFI_SSID=""
WIFI_PASSWORD=""

# --- data wipe ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Wiping is done ON THE KIOSK SCREEN ONLY, one record per drive: pick the
# drive(s), check the model and serial, confirm. See HARDWARE-AUDIT.md,
# "Secure data wipe".
#
# AUDIT_WIPE is RETIRED (owner decision D9, 19 Sep 2026). It used to switch on
# a wipe in the text-mode script that erased every internal drive and filed
# them all as ONE result. It now does nothing but print "wiping is done from
# the kiosk screen" - no drive is erased by the text-mode script whatever it
# is set to. Delete the line from old audit.conf files; leaving it is harmless.
#
# Default method the kiosk pre-selects (the operator can still change it per
# wipe; changing the DEFAULT from the Settings screen needs the admin PIN):
#   auto      = the drive's own cryptographic erase if supported, else its
#               firmware secure erase, else overwrite (default)
#   crypto    = cryptographic erase (self-encrypting / NVMe), else overwrite
#   secure    = firmware secure erase (ATA / NVMe), else overwrite
#   overwrite = random pass + zero pass, read back (slowest, most compatible)
#   zero      = single zero pass, read back (NIST Clear, half the time)
AUDIT_WIPE_METHOD="auto"
# SATA drives are usually "frozen" by the BIOS after boot, which blocks ATA
# secure erase. Set to "1" to briefly suspend/resume to unfreeze — but some
# machines don't resume from suspend, so leave "0" unless you've tested it.
# (Owner decision D42: stays off; a frozen drive is overwritten instead.)
AUDIT_WIPE_UNFREEZE="0"

# --- OS image library -------------------------------------------------------
# Where installable OS images live. Leave blank to use the /images folder on
# this stick. Set it to a share on your local image server and every station
# reads one shared copy instead of carrying 8-15GB per stick:
#   NFS  ->  192.168.1.50:/srv/als-images
#   SMB  ->  //192.168.1.50/als-images
# Mounted read-only and soft, so an unreachable server can never hang the
# station — it just falls back to the images on the stick.
IMAGE_SERVER=""

# --- time -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audited machines are old and their CMOS batteries are usually dead, so they
# boot with the wrong date — which breaks HTTPS (certificates look "not yet
# valid") and stops audits uploading. The station corrects its clock at every
# boot. Set this to your image server to get exact time with NO internet:
#   TIME_SERVER="192.168.0.20"
# Leave blank and it uses the image server's host, then the internet.
TIME_SERVER=""
